<title>INDIA: Indian soybean firm, oil up, meal weak.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean firm, oil up, meal weak.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained firm on good demand from processing plants. Plants are creating stock because the long holiday for the Hindu festival of Diwali is nearing and the market will be closed.</p>
<p>Prices were up by 100-150 rupees per tonne in markets and plant delivery condition. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up by 300 rupees per tonne on good demand from vanaspati manufacturers. Soyoil refined was steady. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices remained weak on limited export demand and selling was also limited. Soymeal yellow was $260-262 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $125-127 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,300 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,250-4,275 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
